  "request": {
    "spec": "The sheet's settings assign a role to a user name: clerk (the default for any name) or steward\n(ROLE_SET user=<name> role=<role>). The sheet also has a clerk limit (two decimals; blank means no\nlimit; SETTING_CHANGED key=clerk-limit value=<limit>). A clerk can settle a claim only when its\ndue is at or below the limit; above it, settling is refused with an error on the claim. Stewards\nsettle anything. The opener still cannot settle their own claim.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nThe sheet's settings assign a role to a user name: clerk (the default for any name) or steward\n(ROLE_SET user=<name> role=<role>). The sheet also has a clerk limit (two decimals; blank means no\nlimit; SETTING_CHANGED key=clerk-limit value=<limit>). A clerk can settle a claim only when its\ndue is at or below the limit; above it, settling is refused with an error on the claim. Stewards\nsettle anything. The opener still cannot settle their own claim.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
